{"event": "PostToolUse", "payload": {"session_id": "2089523e-d6bf-4039-a489-88a16a172507", "transcript_path": "${CONFIG}/projects/-work/2089523e-d6bf-4039-a489-88a16a172507.jsonl", "cwd": "${WORK}", "scratchpad_dir": "${WORK}/scratchpad", "prompt_id": "9812954d-0227-47a7-869e-abb2932ff6d4", "permission_mode": "default", "effort": {"level": "medium"}, "hook_event_name": "PostToolUse", "tool_name": "WebSearch", "tool_input": {"query": "IANA example domain", "mode": "standard"}, "tool_response": {"query": "IANA example domain", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_01PySM7bnDeaFxR6sv4u8nNu", "content": [{"title": "0% found this document useful (0 votes)", "url": "https://www.scribd.com/document/873956284/Example-Domains"}, {"title": ".example", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/.example"}, {"title": "www.example.com - dns.ninja", "url": "https://dns.ninja/en/dns-lookup/com/example/www"}, {"title": "info44.example.com - dns.ninja", "url": "https://dns.ninja/en/dns-lookup/com/example/info44"}, {"title": "www.wikipedia.org", "url": "https://Www.wikipedia.org/wiki/Example.com"}, {"title": "m.example.com - robtex.com", "url": "https://robtex.com/en/dns-lookup/com/example/m"}, {"title": "IANA-managed Reserved Domains", "url": "https://res-dom.iana.org"}, {"title": "example domains", "url": "https://www.netify.ai/documentation/netify-agent/v4/integration_resources/applications/catalog/example-domains"}, {"title": "The domains example.com, example.net, and", "url": "https://kottke.org/02/03/the-domains-examplecom-examplenet-and"}, {"title": "Example Domains", "url": "https://www.netify.ai/documentation/agent/concepts/features/applications/catalog/example-domains"}]}, "The official IANA page is the most authoritative source here. It says IANA maintains a set of example domains, such as example.com and example.org, for documentation. Per RFC 2606 and RFC 6761, these names serve as illustrative examples in documents, and you don't need to coordinate with IANA to use them. Registration and transfer aren't possible. IANA also runs a basic informational web service on these hosts, though it's offered on a best-effort basis and isn't meant for production use (IANA-managed Reserved Domains).\n\nThe domains example.com, example.net, and example.org are the main ones. Wikipedia notes that the label has been reserved and registered since at least 1992, and that the IETF formalized this use in 1999 (Wikipedia, example.com). Separately, the top-level name \".example\" is reserved so it can't be installed in the DNS root. It's a reserved TLD with no registrations possible (Wikipedia, .example).\n\nSome third-party sites (such as dns.ninja and Robtex) repeat these same facts, but they add little beyond the IANA page and sometimes contain unsourced details, so I'd rely on the IANA and RFC documents for accuracy."], "durationSeconds": 5.295296375, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_use_id": "toolu_01SNTn5vWZzEzYXMw1vWG16c", "duration_ms": 5296}}
